{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And may He give you the blessing of Abraham.</b> As it says: וֶהְיֵה בְּרָכָה (Genesis 12:2) — and this is by teaching the people knowledge, and through this the blessing of El, blessed be He, will be <b>to you and to your seed with you, to inherit</b>. For when the seed too instructs righteousness, it will be worthy to inherit, and through this there will be sanctification of HaShem — not its opposite. As it says: יִשְׂרָאֵל אֲשֶׁר בְּךָ אֶתְפָּאָר (Isaiah 49:3), for through this HaShem rejoices in His works." "<b>The land of your sojournings.</b> The land of Canaan, in which you now dwell."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {0 "The lemma break at לְךָ וּלְזַרְעֲךָ is placed mid-sentence within the same comment; kept as Sforno gives it."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:32:08.664763890Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}